# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for vb_tests.
#
# GameNetworkingSockets (FetchContent'd in cmake/Dependencies.cmake) is
# never linked against vb_sanitizers (see that target's own comment in
# Sanitizers.cmake) -- like every other vendored dependency, it is not
# recompiled with -fsanitize=thread. TSan's lock-state shadow tracking
# for its recursive-mutex wrappers (SteamNetworkingSocketsLib::Lock<>/
# ScopeLock<>) loses sync across that instrumentation boundary, reporting
# "unlock of an unlocked mutex", lock-order-inversion, and memcpy races
# that are entirely internal to GNS's own locking and never observed with
# ASan/UBSan (which do run clean against it, modulo the array-bounds/
# conversion carve-outs already documented in Sanitizers.cmake). Same
# class of false positive as that ASan carve-out, just TSan's version of
# it -- not a real race in this codebase.
#
# Wired in via TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file> (see
# .github/workflows/build_linux.yml's tsan leg).
mutex:SteamNetworkingSocketsLib::
deadlock:SteamNetworkingSocketsLib::
race:SteamNetworkingSocketsLib::
